1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,410
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:08,050
You want me to leave?

4
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:11,320
Are you firing me right now?

5
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:24,160
I am sorry for not
meeting your expectations.

6
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,300
I will get going, then.

7
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:00,230
She actually left.

8
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,210
First he tells me to do nothing
and just watch,

9
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,840
and then he dumps
an impossible task on me...

10
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,010
and tells me to leave
if I cannot do it.

11
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,710
He just fired me on the spot.

12
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,380
Then why offer me
the assistant job...

13
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:15,750
in the first place?

14
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:18,920
Ms. Kang Da Mi?

15
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:20,820
Yes, Team Leader Cha.

16
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:23,150
Judging by your expression,

17
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:24,290
it looks like you had
a really rough day.

18
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,260
Being an assistant
is not easy, is it?

19
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,490
Well...

20
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:42,640
Here, drink this.

21
00:01:43,110 --> 00:01:44,280
Thank you.

22
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,350
To be honest,

23
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,480
I was just fired.

24
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,420
Why? Seung Yun...

25
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,020
I thought the head designer...

26
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,120
offered you the job first.

27
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,660
I know you two are brothers.

28
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:01,090
You do not have to
speak so formally.

29
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,190
Still, we are at the company.

30
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,930
Did you make
some sort of big mistake?

31
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,100
No.

32
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,970
All I did all day
was clean the office...

33
00:02:10,970 --> 00:02:12,740
and watch him work.

34
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:16,770
Then out of nowhere, he gave me
a really difficult assignment,

35
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,180
so I was completely
caught off guard.

36
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:21,010
I just felt so lost,

37
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,210
not knowing what to do
or where to start.

38
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:24,080
That is too harsh.

39
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:27,520
So he really told you
that he could not work with you...

40
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:30,520
- and not to come back?
- I have worked all kinds...

41
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:32,190
of part-time jobs,

42
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:35,030
and I have worked
at a department store for years,

43
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:38,960
but this is truly a first for me.

44
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:43,070
This is my first time working
in the same space with him as well,

45
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,940
so I am a bit hesitant
to give advice, but...

46
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,110
Please do.

47
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,540
Honestly, I want to
ask him point-blank...

48
00:02:48,610 --> 00:02:50,440
what the real reason is.

49
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,840
That is it.

50
00:02:53,610 --> 00:02:56,010
- What is?
- Designers at fashion companies,

51
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:59,750
especially head designers,
do not easily hire team members...

52
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,220
who will work right
by their side all day.

53
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:04,090
And Head Designer Cha Seung Yun
is even more meticulous by nature.

54
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,320
So telling you not to come back...

55
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,990
after observing you
for just one day...

56
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:12,160
He might have meant it,
but could he be testing you instead?

57
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,800
How can I find that out?

58
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,340
Even if you end up fired anyway,

59
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,570
would it not be better
to ask him for the exact reason?

60
00:03:21,870 --> 00:03:23,310
That way, you will not feel
so frustrated...

61
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,440
or feel like it was unfair.

62
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:37,920
I need to find the cause
so I can rework the sample quickly.

63
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:42,830
What could it really be?

64
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:53,270
Are you heading home now,
Head Designer Cha?

65
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:56,980
Didn't you walk out earlier,
saying you were quitting?

66
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,310
Why are you still out here
at this hour?

67
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,780
Don't tell me
you were waiting for me?

68
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,380
Even if I get fired,
I wanted to know the exact reason...

69
00:04:03,510 --> 00:04:06,120
- before going home.
- Wait, did I fire you?

70
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:08,820
Didn't you just jump to conclusions
all by yourself, Kang Da Mi?

71
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:14,560
When I asked if you were firing me,
you clearly nodded your head.

72
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:19,330
That just meant you could leave
if you wanted to quit.

73
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,670
I meant you were free
to do as you pleased.

74
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:25,070
Well, if you had
just spoken clearly,

75
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:28,210
I wouldn't have thought I was fired
and walked out in the first place.

76
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:32,840
You just nodded,
so of course I thought I was fired.

77
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:34,550
It was quitting time,

78
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:36,080
so I simply told you
to head home early.

79
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,920
Besides, Kang Da Mi,
if you want to know what it means...

80
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,990
when I nod like this,

81
00:04:41,050 --> 00:04:42,750
ask me properly
right then and there.

82
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,520
Then I will give you a clear answer.

83
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:47,160
Don't just jump to conclusions
and decide...

84
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:49,260
everything on your own, understand?

85
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,600
Yes.

86
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:53,730
Then can I really
keep coming to work...

87
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,200
See you tomorrow.

88
00:04:57,970 --> 00:04:59,570
See you tomorrow, Head Designer Cha.

89
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:16,420
Mrs. Anseong, is Mother asleep?

90
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:19,290
She took a quick nap earlier,
but she is awake again.

91
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,490
Are you going in? Shall I bring tea?

92
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,000
If she keeps sleeping
in the early evening,

93
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,860
she will struggle through the night.

94
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:29,470
No tea, thanks.
I will just see her for a moment.

95
00:05:40,550 --> 00:05:42,150
Are you looking into it?

96
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:46,050
Yes, but it might take a few days.

97
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:49,450
I see. I don't know
why I brushed it off...

98
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,660
so easily in the beginning.

99
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:54,330
I'm sorry for rushing you.

100
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:57,430
Please consider it a favor...

101
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,760
for someone who doesn't
have much time left.

102
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,370
The name Jeon Jin Sook...

103
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,440
Are you sure that is
what you heard, Madam Chairwoman?

104
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:08,310
Well, that's how I remember it,

105
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:12,340
though it could have been
Jeong Jin Sook.

106
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,980
Or maybe it was Jeong Jin Ju,

107
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:19,120
and my memory
is playing tricks on me.

108
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:24,120
Please keep every possibility open
and look into it for me.

109
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,920
I will wait for your call.

110
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,430
Yes, Madam Chairwoman,
I will keep in touch.

111
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,160
All right.

112
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:48,410
Who on earth
could she be looking for?

113
00:06:54,350 --> 00:06:57,460
- I'm home, honey.
- You're very late.

114
00:06:57,790 --> 00:07:00,020
I was getting worried
and was just about to call you.

115
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:03,490
Mother is still awake, right?
I will say hello to her first.

116
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,400
She seems to be
on an important call.

117
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:08,270
I decided not to go in either.

118
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,900
An important call?

119
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,700
Yes.

120
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:19,680
Mother...

121
00:07:20,210 --> 00:07:23,110
She rarely gives work orders
late at night, does she?

122
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:24,850
You said her memory
is not what it used to be.

123
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,450
What could it be, honey?

124
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:29,850
I only overheard for a moment
at the door,

125
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,560
so I do not know for sure.

126
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,760
You know how I told you...

127
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:37,090
Mother asked Dr. Ju separately
to look for someone?

128
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:38,930
Yes.

129
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:42,300
Did you hear who she is looking for?

130
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:46,570
Jeong Jin Sook, Jeong Jin Ju,
or something like that.

131
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,840
She could not seem to remember
the name correctly.

132
00:07:50,610 --> 00:07:54,310
How much money
could they have taken from her...

133
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,680
for her to be tracking them down
at her age?

134
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,980
Did you say you heard
Jeong Jin Sook, honey?

135
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:02,420
Yes, that is what it sounded like.

136
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:05,620
You must be tired.
Go wash up and rest.

137
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:07,590
I will pour us some wine.

138
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:09,560
A glass would be nice
before bed, right?

139
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:11,730
Thank you, honey.

140
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:18,670
Jeong Jin Sook?

141
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,910
She is looking for Jeong Jin Sook?

142
00:08:24,610 --> 00:08:26,710
The person she is looking for
is Jeong Jin Sook?

143
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:30,150
Is that you, Do Yun's mother?

144
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:32,380
- Jin Sook.
- What?

145
00:08:32,450 --> 00:08:33,450
Hey, Jeon Jin Sook.

146
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:35,620
Mother, stepping out for fresh air?

147
00:08:37,090 --> 00:08:38,090
Yes.

148
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:39,590
(Aunt)

149
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:42,890
Who is calling
at this hour of the night?

150
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:45,430
Could it be...

151
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,600
That night, that name...

152
00:08:49,370 --> 00:08:50,370
Did she hear it?

153
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,840
Does she still remember it?

154
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:56,770
No.

155
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,940
It cannot be.

156
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,280
If that is the case...

157
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,360
I am so hungry.

158
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:23,670
Right, I did not even get
to eat dinner tonight.

159
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:30,370
How am I supposed to figure that out
in 48 hours?

160
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:33,510
I need to find out
to save my own skin.

161
00:09:41,590 --> 00:09:42,620
I am home.

162
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,820
Where are Grandma and Mom?
Are they asleep?

163
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:50,760
Just go upstairs
and sleep quietly tonight.

164
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:54,070
Your mother was so exhausted...

165
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,630
she passed out
without even having dinner.

166
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,840
Does Mom have body aches?

167
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,910
Since you took my advice
and decided to move out,

168
00:10:02,410 --> 00:10:04,440
listen to me to the end, young lady.

169
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,610
She kept her eyes closed,
so she seemed fast asleep.

170
00:10:09,010 --> 00:10:10,680
Do not go in there and wake her.

171
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:14,850
Mrs. Choi seemed
to turn in early too.

172
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,520
All right.

173
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:22,730
By the way, why are you
drinking soju alone at this hour?

174
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:26,500
I thought you would be the happiest
to hear that I am moving out.

175
00:10:29,030 --> 00:10:32,000
I feel like I need to get drunk
just to fall asleep.

176
00:10:34,310 --> 00:10:36,540
I am glad you are leaving, so...

177
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:38,580
Make sure you leave...

178
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,180
and take some weight
off my sister's shoulders.

179
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:43,310
Still, you cannot just vanish
out of the blue.

180
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:44,950
Leave a letter behind at least.

181
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:48,650
I really do not want my sister
to resent me.

182
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:50,890
Get some sleep.

183
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,260
My poor sister.

184
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:00,800
Those terrible people...

185
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:03,870
I hoped we would never
cross paths with them again.

186
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:12,210
Wait a minute. Should I...

187
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,750
give Mrs. Choi
a subtle hint about this?

188
00:11:21,850 --> 00:11:24,060
I am so tired.

189
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:29,330
I should still pack, right?

190
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:41,940
All right.

191
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:02,390
Oh, right.

192
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:11,140
I should take this.

193
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,790
You guys come with me too.

194
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,190
Still, you cannot just vanish
out of the blue.

195
00:12:36,530 --> 00:12:37,860
Leave a letter behind at least.

196
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:41,530
I really do not want my sister
to resent me.

197
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:45,370
This is what Mom wanted too.

198
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,940
And now, it is what I want as well.

199
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:05,660
(To My Dearest Mom...)

200
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:10,290
I need to write this carefully
so she does not get hurt.

201
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,700
Please do not be upset, Mom.

202
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,530
I am sorry.

203
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,070
What?

204
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:56,610
Sweetheart.

205
00:13:57,210 --> 00:13:58,210
Goodness.

206
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,710
Are you going to work
at the crack of dawn?

207
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,750
Grandma, Mom is still sleeping.

208
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:05,150
I will get going. See you later.

209
00:14:05,450 --> 00:14:07,220
Wait, what is that suitcase for?

210
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:11,960
Well, the new company
I am starting at...

211
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:16,890
is too far from home. So I
decided to stay with a friend...

212
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,560
near the office for a while.

213
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:24,200
Still, how far could it possibly be?
It is still within Seoul, is it not?

214
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,970
Did you tell your mother?

215
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,770
Did she give her permission?

216
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:30,710
Yes, well...

217
00:14:30,770 --> 00:14:34,210
Mom has always nagged me anyway,
telling me to move out already.

218
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:37,450
I should get going, Grandma.

219
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:46,520
Sweetheart.

220
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:48,930
Da Mi.

221
00:14:53,030 --> 00:14:55,170
Leaving on an empty stomach?
My gosh.

222
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,110
Mrs. Choi.

223
00:15:05,010 --> 00:15:06,510
Are you up already?

224
00:15:07,210 --> 00:15:08,210
Yes.

225
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,680
Da Mi just walked out
with a suitcase packed.

226
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,880
She claimed she got permission
from her mother,

227
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:17,620
but what was Ms. Jo thinking,
letting the girl move out?

228
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,620
I know, right?

229
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:23,660
But...

230
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,560
Mrs. Choi.

231
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:33,200
I just do not understand it.

232
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:36,440
Nothing worse could happen now,
so why?

233
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,680
Mrs. Choi,

234
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:40,910
did you really have no idea?

235
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:44,350
I had a feeling about something,
so I wanted to ask.

236
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,990
No idea about what? What feeling?

237
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:50,890
My sister and I...

238
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:53,560
Lately, you've been leaving
without saying a word,

239
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,530
stepping out of the restaurant
so often,

240
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:57,630
and you seemed troubled,

241
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,200
so we've been worried
the whole time.

242
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:03,030
You knew all along, didn't you?

243
00:16:03,370 --> 00:16:06,100
Get to the point.
Stop driving me crazy.

244
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:07,640
What do I know?

245
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:10,940
My brother-in-law
and that woman's family.

246
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,980
They moved to this neighborhood.

247
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,450
Are you telling me
you truly didn't know?

248
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,350
Mona Ri Ja, how did you find out?

249
00:16:21,090 --> 00:16:22,090
Don't tell me...

250
00:16:22,850 --> 00:16:23,950
Does Mi Mi know too?

251
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:27,360
Good grief. I suspected it,

252
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:29,960
and I was right.

253
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:32,930
Mrs. Choi, how could you
hide that from us?

254
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:35,470
Does Mi Mi know?

255
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:40,840
No, that wretched woman said
she was quitting Dr. Ju's clinic,

256
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:43,070
and Hak Sung told me not to worry.

257
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:46,110
What am I going to do?

258
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,380
Yesterday, Mi Mi...

259
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,920
barely finished closing
and came home,

260
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,990
and she hasn't said a word since.

261
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:59,220
She's lying down facing the wall,
keeping her eyes tightly shut.

262
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:01,020
Why did you do that?

263
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:03,530
Well, you see...

264
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:06,600
I must have lost my mind.

265
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:09,200
He showed up looking like a beggar,

266
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:11,170
so I went to him without thinking.

267
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:17,810
- She must be furious, right?
- Well, rather than furious,

268
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:20,640
wouldn't she feel
completely devastated?

269
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:25,480
She took care of you
like her own mother for decades...

270
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,890
and spent all these years
raising the kids.

271
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:32,490
She's bound to feel
hurt and betrayed.

272
00:17:33,090 --> 00:17:34,760
What are you going to do now?

273
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,100
I have to talk to her.

274
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:42,300
And apologize, too.

275
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:45,470
But she needs to get up
and move around...

276
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,070
for me to even try to talk to her.

277
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,210
Seriously...

278
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:59,980
I only packed the basics,
so why is this so heavy?

279
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,830
Mi Seon.

280
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:14,670
Mi Seon.

281
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:18,440
Da Mi?

282
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:20,940
What are you doing here so early?

283
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:25,080
What a relief. You're actually home.
Can I come in?

284
00:18:27,010 --> 00:18:28,550
What's with the suitcase?

285
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:32,080
I've decided to move out on my own.

286
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:34,950
Well, one of your mother's wishes
came true.

287
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,920
And? Why are you standing here?

288
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:39,790
Because I left in such a hurry,

289
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,690
I haven't had time
to find a place yet.

290
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:43,760
Can I crash here for a bit?

291
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:46,800
Where do you think you're coming in?

292
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:50,500
I just told you,
I haven't found a place yet.

293
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:54,170
You moved out without even finding
an apartment first?

294
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:56,070
Yes.

295
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:58,880
- The thing is...
- Stop.

296
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,850
I am divorced,
so I am your ex-sister-in-law.

297
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:05,780
I even left Su Ah behind
and am trying so hard...

298
00:19:05,850 --> 00:19:08,390
to distance myself
from the Kang family.

299
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:09,590
How could you
just barge in like this...

300
00:19:09,650 --> 00:19:10,650
without giving me any warning?

301
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,820
This room is too small
even for just me.

302
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:17,190
What am I supposed to do then?

303
00:19:17,390 --> 00:19:18,600
I just wanted to leave
my suitcase here...

304
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:20,260
and head straight to work.

305
00:19:24,130 --> 00:19:27,000
Oh, right. I have every right...

306
00:19:27,070 --> 00:19:29,570
to stay here for a while.

307
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:33,180
What right?

308
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,410
I gave you the 10,000 dollars
for the deposit.

309
00:19:38,850 --> 00:19:41,390
So you expect me
to pay you back like this?

310
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,230
Let us talk after work.

311
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:52,160
Thank you.
Just put my suitcase inside for now.

312
00:19:52,430 --> 00:19:53,500
I am off.

313
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,830
I am your ex-sister-in-law.

314
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:01,040
What am I going to do?

315
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:08,710
Excuse me.

316
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,080
Me?

317
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,850
You know. Why even ask?

318
00:20:14,550 --> 00:20:15,720
You turned down Team Leader Cha...

319
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:17,650
when he offered you
a manager position...

320
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,720
at the pop-up store.

321
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:22,730
So why on earth did you agree
to be the head designer's assistant?

322
00:20:23,790 --> 00:20:26,060
Did you forget what kind of person
our CEO is?

323
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:29,500
Forget? She is CEO Jeon Jin Hee.

324
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,400
And do you also remember...

325
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:34,770
that our CEO
is not pleased with you?

326
00:20:36,170 --> 00:20:37,170
Yes.

327
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:38,940
I could tell she was not happy
to see me...

328
00:20:39,010 --> 00:20:42,050
from the moment I saw her yesterday.
It is just that I...

329
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:43,980
Go on.

330
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:48,420
I know very well that CEO Jeon
does not have fond memories of me.

331
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:50,720
I hesitated as well,

332
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:52,160
but I wanted a chance to work...

333
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:55,460
under a famous designer
who made it in the US.

334
00:20:56,230 --> 00:20:57,460
Does that answer your question?

335
00:20:57,930 --> 00:21:01,060
How do you even know
Head Designer Cha Seung Yun?

336
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:05,400
How did you catch his eye
and land this assistant position?

337
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:07,400
I am dying to know.

338
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:08,810
(Head Designer's Office)

339
00:21:08,870 --> 00:21:11,210
Wouldn't it be better...

340
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,610
to ask Head Designer Cha
directly instead of me?

341
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:20,320
- So you do not want to tell me?
- It is not that.

342
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:22,590
I just think it would be
more accurate...

343
00:21:22,650 --> 00:21:24,290
to hear the reason from
Head Designer Cha himself.

344
00:21:25,490 --> 00:21:28,660
Is that so?
Fine, I will ask him myself.

345
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:29,960
Still,

346
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:32,900
try to hang in there
until I hear his reason.

347
00:21:33,530 --> 00:21:35,130
He is not an easy person
to deal with.

348
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,100
Just a piece of advice.

349
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,070
Excuse me, Assistant Manager.

350
00:21:42,910 --> 00:21:47,210
My name is Kang Da Mi, not "you."

351
00:21:48,010 --> 00:21:49,080
Have a good day.

352
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:51,780
Who does she think she is?

353
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:53,580
She should be trying
to get on my good side,

354
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:54,650
not lecturing me.

355
00:21:56,950 --> 00:21:58,460
You are all in early.

356
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:01,090
We needed to prep in advance...

357
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:02,830
to welcome the Summit investors,
Team Leader Cha.

358
00:22:03,630 --> 00:22:05,830
- Good morning, Head Designer Cha.
- Yes, good morning.

359
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,330
What are you doing?
Aren't you coming in?

360
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:09,930
Yes, sir.

361
00:22:10,430 --> 00:22:11,440
Oh, Head Designer Cha.

362
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:15,410
Ms. Kang Da Mi is new
as an assistant,

363
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:16,410
so please take good care of her.

364
00:22:16,910 --> 00:22:19,340
Wait, shouldn't I be
the one saying that...

365
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:20,440
to the Product Planning team?

366
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:23,650
Come to think of it, you're right.

367
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:29,490
Even if she's a bit inexperienced,
please help her out.

368
00:22:29,820 --> 00:22:31,920
Though I don't know
how long we'll be working together.

369
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:35,460
Indeed.
I hope you hang in there, Da Mi.

370
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:39,100
If you ever have trouble,
feel free to ask for help anytime.

371
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,130
Yes.

372
00:22:42,630 --> 00:22:45,840
That is very reassuring. Thank you.

373
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:49,640
She was someone I wanted on my team,

374
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:51,440
so please take good care of her.

375
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:54,080
Right.

376
00:22:55,310 --> 00:22:56,350
Excuse me.

377
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:00,880
Good luck to you.

378
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:08,730
So pretty.

379
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:15,500
Even if you're working from home,

380
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:17,430
aren't you slacking off
way too much?

381
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:20,100
Mom helped put out
the immediate fire,

382
00:23:20,170 --> 00:23:21,470
but you still have to
pay back the debt.

383
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:25,540
Is staring at that phone all day
going to pay your salary?

384
00:23:25,910 --> 00:23:27,980
Mind your own business
and take Su Ah to school.

385
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:33,080
Hey, even if your debt is
1,130,000 dollars,

386
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:37,290
aren't you being too oblivious
to what's happening at home?

387
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:40,560
Do you have any idea
what it's like downstairs?

388
00:23:42,330 --> 00:23:43,490
Hey, Kang Dae Chi.

389
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,430
Let me tell you what
happened yesterday.

390
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:52,370
Do you know
who came by the restaurant?

391
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:56,010
I need to take an important call.

392
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,310
Su Ah, have a good day
at kindergarten.

393
00:23:58,380 --> 00:23:59,380
Go on now. Quick, hurry.

394
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:00,810
- What is it?
- Hurry up, please.

395
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:02,950
- Aren't you curious?
- Get out, quickly.

396
00:24:10,050 --> 00:24:13,320
Yes, this is Manager Kang Dae Chi
of Purchasing.

397
00:24:16,430 --> 00:24:18,560
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

398
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:22,600
You really have no shame, do you?

399
00:24:22,700 --> 00:24:23,900
Let's not do this.

400
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:27,770
I met with Mom yesterday
and made a promise.

401
00:24:28,210 --> 00:24:29,970
Even if we can't afford
to move right away,

402
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,810
I promised you'd quit this clinic.

403
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:35,910
Honey, can't you see this bald spot
on my head?

404
00:24:36,910 --> 00:24:38,420
To say the least,

405
00:24:38,550 --> 00:24:40,220
she must have pulled out
over 1,000 hairs.

406
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:42,920
After having my hair pulled,
why quit?

407
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,590
I'm going to make every penny I can.

408
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:48,290
Besides, at my age,
is a job like this easy to find?

409
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:52,660
Instead, I'll earn
more money for us.

410
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:53,860
Please, Ye Ri's mom.

411
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:56,400
You said yourself...

412
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:57,970
the clinic pays you minimum wage
anyway.

413
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:02,340
Dr. Ju must have noticed
that I was having second thoughts,

414
00:25:02,410 --> 00:25:04,710
because he offered me
a raise of 500 dollars.

415
00:25:06,410 --> 00:25:07,410
Five hundred dollars?

416
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:11,310
Yes, so I'm going to grab that money
and save every single cent.

417
00:25:11,450 --> 00:25:14,150
- So don't you try to stop me.
- Honey, wait.

418
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:18,990
She was never such a stubborn woman,
my Park Ji Young...

419
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:22,460
Good grief. Money really is
the root of all evil.

420
00:25:24,590 --> 00:25:26,300
What do I do now?

421
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:33,240
I gave Mom my word...

422
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:57,830
(Mom)

423
00:26:06,270 --> 00:26:08,200
If it's urgent,
you may step outside to take it.

424
00:26:08,740 --> 00:26:10,440
No, it's fine.

425
00:26:13,180 --> 00:26:14,580
Have you given it any thought?

426
00:26:16,050 --> 00:26:17,080
Pardon?

427
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:18,980
About the first assignment
I gave you.

428
00:26:19,650 --> 00:26:22,320
Out of the 48 hours,
quite a few have already passed.

429
00:26:25,320 --> 00:26:26,320
Well...

430
00:26:28,390 --> 00:26:29,390
Ms. Kang Da Mi,

431
00:26:30,260 --> 00:26:33,130
I didn't hire you as my assistant...

432
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:35,770
just to clean up around here
and organize things.

433
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:38,130
Don't just stick to what's familiar.

434
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,800
Really dive into it
and grapple with the problem.

435
00:26:40,740 --> 00:26:41,770
Time is running out.

436
00:26:43,870 --> 00:26:44,870
Yes, sir.

437
00:26:48,610 --> 00:26:50,310
The person you have called
is unavailable.

438
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:52,120
Please leave a message
after the tone...

439
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:58,990
(To My Dearest Mom...)

440
00:26:58,990 --> 00:27:00,020
(Mom, you’re already having
a hard time with my brothers...)

441
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:04,390
What on earth did she write
before leaving?

442
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:08,230
"Thank you for everything"?

443
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,170
"Thank you for raising me"?

444
00:27:18,110 --> 00:27:19,940
Didn't I tell you
to leave Da Mi alone?

445
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:23,680
What did you say to her
to make her run away from home?

446
00:27:25,550 --> 00:27:26,620
Mi Mi.

447
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:34,260
Da Mi left the house.

448
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:38,560
She packed her bags
and left early this morning.

449
00:27:39,330 --> 00:27:43,470
- She said she got your permission.
- While Da Mi was packing to leave,

450
00:27:44,070 --> 00:27:46,100
Mother, you should have woken me up.

451
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,570
If you just let her go,
what am I supposed to do?

452
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:52,510
After all the years
we lived together,

453
00:27:54,210 --> 00:27:57,750
how could you fail to understand
how I feel?

454
00:28:13,230 --> 00:28:15,130
(Mission: Mompossible)

455
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:16,670
It's 10,000 dollars.

456
00:28:16,670 --> 00:28:20,540
Take that money and prove yourself
by leaving our neighborhood now.

457
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:22,440
These are last year's
spring-summer season...

458
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:23,670
sales figures by category.

459
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,840
Why is Team Leader Cha
being so nice to her?

460
00:28:26,110 --> 00:28:30,610
Mother, do you know why
I married your son?

461
00:28:31,850 --> 00:28:33,850
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
